# Everything the image does not need, and a few things it must not have.
#
# The build copies what the Dockerfile names: the manifests, the tsconfigs and the Vite config, the build's two scripts,
# and src/. Anything else in the tree is either rebuilt inside the image, irrelevant to it, or a secret.

# Rebuilt in the image. Copying a host build would put macOS/musl-mismatched artifacts and the whole toolchain into the layer.
node_modules
dist
**/node_modules
desktop/node_modules
desktop/release
desktop/build

# History and metadata. .git in particular is both large and a leak: it holds every version of every file that was ever
# committed, including ones deleted since.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local notes and editor state.
.notes
.claude
.idea

# The demo database and anything else generated by running the tool. These are real databases someone pointed tablewalk at.
.demo
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Credentials, in every form they show up in.
.env
.env.*
tablewalk.json
.tablewalk.json
credentials.json
*.pem
*.key

# Project documents. They are not wrong to ship, they are just weight.
docs
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
SECURITY.md
CLAUDE.md

# Tests and their fixtures.
e2e
test
.visual

# Docker's own files: changing the compose file should not invalidate the build cache for the source.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml

*.log
.DS_Store
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
